{
  "_doc": "bugs_open/309 candidate 2 - the FROZEN grandfather baseline for the at-rest source-vocabulary audit. DERIVED FROM THE SHIPPED RULE via `config-key-audit --component-source-vocabulary --emit-baseline`, never hand-written and never from a re-implementation of the classification (the first cut was generated by a SQL restatement of the rule, which the council's debug_historian seat correctly objected to: a baseline built by a second predicate is the very drift this mode exists to prevent, arriving through the back door). THIS FILE MAY ONLY EVER SHRINK. It is keyed on the exact (component_id, field, source, class) tuple, so an entry can only excuse the one finding it was written for - a changed source on the same field, or a new bad field on the same component, is a NEW finding and turns the job red. Every entry is dated 2026-08-22 and the loader REFUSES any other date: the baseline is closed, and a new finding is fixed or routed, never baselined. Grandfathering is CONDITIONAL for the dormant components (live_instances_at_baseline = 0): if one is deployed, the job goes red. An entry matching nothing live is STALE and also turns the job red - that is the ratchet's pawl, and it is how repairs burn this file down. Being here downgrades the EXIT CODE and never the REPORT: the daily doc_notes row names the whole population every run.",
